---
title: Empty
description: A container for displaying empty state information.
---

<ComponentPreview name="p-empty-1" />

## Installation

<InstallCommand pnpm="pnpm add @shardsui/svelte" shadcnSvelte="pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/empty.json" />

## Usage

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { Button } from "@coss-sv/ui/components/ui/button";
  import {
    Empty,
    EmptyContent,
    EmptyDescription,
    EmptyHeader,
    EmptyMedia,
    EmptyTitle,
  } from "@coss-sv/ui/components/ui/empty";
</script>

<Empty>
  <EmptyHeader>
    <EmptyMedia variant="icon">Icon</EmptyMedia>
    <EmptyTitle>No data</EmptyTitle>
    <EmptyDescription>No data found</EmptyDescription>
  </EmptyHeader>
  <EmptyContent>
    <Button>Add data</Button>
  </EmptyContent>
</Empty>
```

## API Reference

This API follows the familiar shadcn/ui empty-state composition. Every part accepts native `div`
attributes, snippets, `class`, and a bindable `ref`.

### Empty

The empty-state root. It wraps `EmptyHeader` and `EmptyContent`.

### EmptyHeader

Groups the media, title, and description.

### EmptyMedia

Displays an icon, image, avatar, or another visual. The `icon` variant adds the COSS layered media
treatment.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `variant` | `"default" \| "icon"` | `"default"` |

### EmptyTitle

The empty-state title.

### EmptyDescription

Supporting text for the empty state.

### EmptyContent

Actions or other supporting controls for the empty state.
